{"id":212211661389222,"type":"album","name":"Come In","artist":"Weatherday","year":2019,"weight":16,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/151267-come-in.jpg","aoty":70,"aoty_user":82,"yt":"5uYKbZ_aJBE","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/weatherday/come-in","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/151267-weatherday-come-in.php"},"desc":"\"Come In\" is Weatherday's debut album, released in 2019 and welcomed by the indie rock community. Sputnik, the creative genius behind Weatherday, cites emo and classical music (from the Classical and Romantic era) as inspiration. Several fans assume Car Seat Headrest's \"Twin Fantasy\" as an obvious source of inspiration, but Sputnik denies that \"Twin Fantasy\" had conscious influence over \"Come In.\" However, what should be mentioned is that the character on the album cover, Mio, derives from Sputnik's now-abolished webcomic that explores foreign identity. Sputnik's webcomic is also a huge inspiration to \"Come In.\" In the article, \"Sonemic Interview: Weatherday/Lola's ."},"artist_ref":{"id":273186773616385,"name":"Weatherday","info":{"img":null}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2333,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":218004892059785,"type":"genre","name":"Emo","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":583,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":7260641021881,"type":"genre","name":"Noise Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":241,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":32298008141495,"type":"genre","name":"Slacker Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":214,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":144321848166418,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Noise Pop","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list